1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,880
Why do you feel broke, even after your paycheck hits your account?

2
00:00:03,880 --> 00:00:11,300
For years, you've done everything right — budgeting, saving, even tithing — but the stress never seems to disappear.

3
00:00:11,300 --> 00:00:13,740
Think about the Parable of the Talents.

4
00:00:13,740 --> 00:00:17,890
Scripture reminds us that a wise steward doesn't chase quick riches.

5
00:00:17,890 --> 00:00:21,150
They build slowly, with patience and diligence.

6
00:00:21,150 --> 00:00:23,020
Let's make this practical.

7
00:00:23,020 --> 00:00:29,930
If you're carrying three thousand dollars in credit card debt, start with just one extra payment of fifty dollars this month.

8
00:00:29,930 --> 00:00:31,000
That's it.

9
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:34,610
Small, faithful steps compound over time.

10
00:00:34,610 --> 00:00:39,760
Lord, thank you for walking with us through every financial season.

11
00:00:39,760 --> 00:00:45,650
Give us the wisdom to manage what You've entrusted to us, and the peace to trust You with the rest.

12
00:00:45,650 --> 00:00:47,100
Amen.
